1. Definitions

   "WestCode Material" means the source code, build scripts, assets and
   documentation in this repository that the Licensor wrote or owns, and the
   parts of any binary built from them. It excludes Third-Party Components.
   "Third-Party Components" means components written by others and included
   in this repository or in a binary, each under its own licence.
   "Software" means WestCode Material together with the Third-Party
   Components as combined in this repository or in a binary.
   "Modification" means a derivative work of WestCode Material within the
   meaning of the South African Copyright Act 98 of 1978, or a copy of a
   substantial part of WestCode Material. It does not include fair quotation
   for criticism, review or user documentation.
   "Contribution" means a Modification you submit to the Licensor's official
   repository, for example as a pull request.
   "Personal Use" means use by a natural person for that person's own
   purposes, with no commercial advantage or monetary compensation sought.
   "Business Use" means any use by or for a company, organisation, sole
   trader or other undertaking, including internal use by its staff, other
   than the work described in section 2(g).
   "Sell" means to charge, or to take advertising revenue, for the Software,
   a Modification, access to or hosting of either, or any product or service
   of which either is a part; or to offer paid support, warranty or indemnity
   whose subject is either. It does not include wages from an employer that
   holds permission under section 4, or genuinely independent advice that
   does not transfer or host the Software.

